goer@quads.uchicago.edu (Richard L. Goerwitz) writes:
]>"What good are things like potions that destroy armor?"

Various people have answered with ways to use bad things.
I'd answer the question differently, though - not everybody in the
dungeon is there just to be nice to YOU, and not everything they do
is friendly.  Monsters try to kill you and eat you - what use is that?
Soldiers plant land-mines.  Other people plant other traps.
Maybe they're trying to kill you.  Maybe they're trying to stop
people from killing them or ripping them off.  Maybe they're just nasty.

Maybe some magic user placed a curse on his items, that it would
backfire on whoever stole it.  And you stole it.  Or you killed
someone who had stolen it.  Maybe you're not so nice yourself!

Maybe some local resident got murdered and ripped off, and the local
priest placed a curse on whoever did it.  Maybe the local priest is
chaotic evil, and is trying to find some sacrificial victims.

Or maybe the local shopkeeper keeps a bunch of poison and
destroy-armor potions around to discourage shoplifters from ripping
off stuff.    *I'd* certainly never do anything like that :-)!


